    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This CD-ROM is a digital copy of the Ives Report. According to the Wagner- Camp Western Americana bibliographic reference (1982) there were three different versions published: the Senate, House, and War Department versions. Wagner-Camp credits the House version as the only source to include Newberry’s Geologic Maps. However, searches through book sources along the Colorado Front Range and on the Internet suggest a different conclusion. Numerous volumes have collation problems – some missing pages, some repeated chapters, some with plates out of place or missing, and all too commonly, missing the maps. Curiously, no inspected House versions included the Newberry Geology Maps, but a couple copies of the Senate version did. USGS librarians and Philip Panum of the Western History Library of the Denver Public Library suggest the publication date of 1861 holds the key. The focus of attention was distracted by the shadow of war. Collations were hastily assembled and bound with available maps and illustrations. It’s likely that the printing of the geology maps was running behind schedule. This CD-ROM was made from a copy of a Senate version from the USGS Library in Denver. Topographical map #1 is from the USGS Denver Library. Topographical map #2 is from the Library of Congress. USGS geologist Scott Minor provided the two geological maps.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
